=== component-traceability v2.0 (sequence 2) hardening-pass evidence ===
Committed on the same local two-organisation Fabric test-network (later
extended with Org3/RegulatorMSP) used throughout this repository, replacing
v1.0/sequence 1. This run demonstrates the four fixes made in response to
supervisor feedback on the second draft:

  1. Off-chain report exposure: RegisterComponent/RecordTest now take a
     client-computed SHA-256 hex digest (testReportHash) as an argument
     instead of the report text itself, so the report is never sent to, or
     visible in, a transaction proposal.
  2. Cross-batch product assembly: RecordAssembly no longer requires every
     component to share one batch (Batch -> Component -> Product/Vehicle ->
     Dealer). PRODUCT-Z below is deliberately assembled from components in
     two different batches (BATCH-Z1, BATCH-Z2) and is indexed under both.
  3. Recall/lifecycle separation: recall status is tracked in a new
     recallStatus field, entirely separate from the lifecycle status field.
     TriggerRecall never touches lifecycle status; RevokeRecall clears
     recallStatus without resetting lifecycle status to a generic
     placeholder, unlike the version evaluated in the first draft.
  4. CounterfeitScan renamed to ProvenanceCheck, since the original name
     implied a stronger guarantee (physical authenticity) than the function
     verifies (ledger presence and declared co-attestation).

Console output below is unedited peer chaincode invoke/query output against
the real network, captured in a single run.
